# Host facts for the wiki stack.
#
# Edit this file, not .env. On oracle this file IS the .env: README.md copies
# it to /opt/wiki/.env unchanged, because `make up STACK=wiki` and
# scripts/render-config.sh do not run on that host (compose.yaml's header says
# why). There is no secrets file for this stack, by the same decision as
# stacks/media's (#528): oracle holds no age identity (ADR-0015).

# The file Wiki.js reads the database password from, on the HOST. It is the one
# secret this stack has, and it lives on oracle alone.
#
# It must be owned by uid 1000 and mode 0400. uid 1000 is `node` inside the
# pinned image and the operator's account on oracle — the same number — so the
# container can read it and no other account on the machine can. Until #251 it
# was 0664, readable by every account on oracle.
#
#   sudo chown 1000:1000 /etc/wiki/.db-secret && sudo chmod 0400 /etc/wiki/.db-secret
#
# The password in it is the `wiki` role's in the cluster. Changing it means
# changing both: ALTER ROLE in the database, then this file, then
# `docker compose up -d --force-recreate app`.
WIKI_DB_SECRET=/etc/wiki/.db-secret

# Left unset. Set ONLY for the one `up` that initialises an empty cluster —
# a restore onto a new volume — and never written into this file; README.md
# § Restore has the procedure. On an initialised cluster Postgres ignores it.
# WIKI_DB_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=
